# Portal OTP flow — phone + 1234 (dev)

Guest registration on **`apps/portal`** (`{club}.portal.{root}`). Authority for P6-1 guest slice.

## Host

Authority: [p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc](p6-host-addressing-architecture.mdoc)

| Env | Portal register / login URL (canonical) | Notes |
| --- | --------------------------------------- | ----- |
| Dev (WRS club) | `http://{club}.portal.localhost:3003/...` | e.g. `denali.portal.localhost:3003` — WRS club-portal form |
| Dev legacy alias | `http://{club}.localhost:3003/...` | Prefer `{club}.portal.localhost` for branding + tenant bind |
| Prod (platform) | `https://{club}.portal.{root}/...` | — |
| Prod (custom apex) | `https://portal.{apex}/...` | e.g. `portal.denali.club` — `tenant_domains` · `surface=portal` |

Marketing CTA resolves portal origin via `resolveWebRegistrationUrl` → **`buildDevPortalPublicBaseUrl`** (`@app-tour/tenant-kernel`; strips `shop.` when present). Custom apex: set `PORTAL_PUBLIC_BASE_URL`.

Wrong host → bootstrap/branding 404. Do not invert apex-style labels on localhost (treat custom-apex `portal.denali.*` separately from WRS `{club}.portal.localhost`).

---

## Coded auth errors (presentation contract · 2026-08-06)

| Code | Meaning | Layer that emits |
| ---- | ------- | ---------------- |
| `MOBILE_REQUIRED` | Phone empty after trim / normalize yields empty | Portal BFF `phone-preflight` · `request-otp` · `verify-otp` |
| `MOBILE_INVALID` | Non-empty phone fails shared `isPublicRegistrationMobileValid(normalize(...))` | Same BFF routes (distinct from required) |
| `OTP_*` / `DISPLAY_NAME_REQUIRED` / … | Unchanged coded failures | BFF ↔ API |

**UI rules (no HTML5 as message source):**

1. Messages resolve only via i18n keys under `catalogRegistration.errors.*` (distinct copy for `MOBILE_REQUIRED` vs `MOBILE_INVALID`).
2. Clear presentation error on input edit (phone / OTP / onboarding profile fields).
3. Onboarding profile form uses `noValidate`; empty name → coded `DISPLAY_NAME_REQUIRED` with `role="alert"` — browser English HTML5 validation must not block submit.
4. Client may mirror the shared normalize/validity helpers from `@app-tour/catalog-registration-auth` before fetch; it must not invent local regex or hard-coded English strings.

---

## Flow (frozen)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[phone] --> B[request OTP]
  B --> C[otp 4 digits]
  C --> D{user exists + ACTIVE membership?}
  D -->|yes| E[intake tour form]
  D -->|no| F[profile: name required · email optional]
  F --> G[register-complete + session]
  G --> E
  E --> H[done success]
```

| Step | UI marker | API |
| ---- | --------- | --- |
| Phone | `data-public-registration-phone` | `POST /api/public-auth/phone-preflight` · `request-otp` |
| OTP | `data-public-registration-otp` | `POST /api/public-auth/verify-otp` |
| Profile (new only) | `data-public-registration-profile` | `POST /api/public-auth/register-complete` |
| Tour intake | `data-public-registration-intake` | `POST /api/catalog/registrations` |
| Success | `data-public-registration-success` | — |

---

## New vs existing user

| Case | After OTP verify |
| ---- | ---------------- |
| **Existing** — mobile in DB + `ACTIVE` membership on tenant | Session cookie set → skip profile → **intake** |
| **New** — no user or no membership | `requires_registration: true` + `onboarding_token` → **profile** → session → **intake** |

Profile rules:

- **Name (`display_name`):** required
- **Email:** optional (omitted in API body when empty)

Tour intake (separate step):

- Name, email, party size required for Denali `POST /denali/registrations` (email is tour contact, not account email).

---

## Dev OTP `1234` (single source)

When `NODE_ENV` is `development` or `test` and `AUTH_ALLOW_DEV_STATIC_OTP !== false`:

| Layer | Mechanism |
| ----- | --------- |
| API challenge | `createMobileOtpChallenge` **issues** static `1234` (same value hashed + logged via `otp-dev delivery`) — not a random 6-digit that disagrees with the UI hint |
| API verify | `verifyMobileOtp` still accepts `1234` (defense-in-depth bypass remains) |
| Portal UI | Pre-fills OTP in dev · `otp.devHint` shows `{code: PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_DEV_OTP}` (`1234`) |
| Shared constant | `PUBLIC_REGISTRATION_DEV_OTP` in `@app-tour/catalog-registration-auth` must match API `DEV_STATIC_OTP` |
| E2E | `CATALOG_DEV_OTP = "1234"` in `catalog-registration-otp.ts` |

When static OTP is disabled (`AUTH_ALLOW_DEV_STATIC_OTP=false`) or production: real OTP from `resolveOtpCodeForChallenge` / SMS (`otp-delivery.ts`); UI must not claim a fixed code.

Decision: **DL-44** in [member-portal-shell/decision-log.mdoc](member-portal-shell/decision-log.mdoc).

